@Contents
$^#colorer library. version 4ever

    it is not enough here.

    ~plugin setup.~@Config@

    ~plugin's menues.~@menu@

    ~about author.~@Author@

    all other information about using colorer read in plugin and library
documentation files.

@Config
$^#colorer's settings.#

  #[x] turn off colorer#
     turns off Colorer - really...

  #[x] log errors (c:\_colorer.log)#
     turns on HRC bases compiling log in #c:\_colorer.log#

  #[x] don't locate hrc directory changes#
     don't use hrc changes autodetection.

  #[x] Cross    [x] Pairs    [x] Syntax#
     turns on/off corresponding features in editor.

  #base file:#
     full file path sets default base file for colorer.
     Leave empty this field shows colorer to search file's
     path in registry.

  #assigns file:#
     path to colors assign file (*.hrd). Works as previous.
     You can set here only filename (without path).

  #[ Reload ]#
     this button reloads hrc base

  #[ Reload all ]#
     this button reloads all hrc base

  #[ Ok ]#
     close dialog

    Really, colorer's formats can reload themself with any
changes in its directory automatically.


@add
$#Menues...
    Here you see list of founded functions or syntax errors. Choosing any line
lets you to go to corresponding line in text.


@menu
$#Colorer operation menues

  #1 List types#          ~Alt-L~
    Lists menu with all supported file types. You can choose any of
them to use with current file in editor.

  #2 Match pair#          ~Alt-[~
    Finds paired bracket (or any other pair structure) to the current under cursor
and jumps there.

  #3 Select block#        ~Alt-]~
    Moves cursor to start of block and selects it all. You can call this
function as on block limits as inside it. In second case colorer will find
start and end of nearest block automatically.

  #4 Select pair#         ~Alt-P~
    Selects pair block - but don't selects pair structures at start and end.

  #5 List functions#      ~Alt-;~
    Searches for functional regions in current file and shows them in menu.
There you can choose and jump into any of them, also you can use there any
alphabetic symbols for creating masks.

  #6 Find errors#         ~Alt-'~
    As previous - but shows all errors in text.

  #*# All these features are depend on content of corresponding HRC files.
All information is taken from syntax regions analyse.

  #7 Select region#       ~Alt-K~
    Selects current color region under cursor.

  #C Configuration#
    Calls colorer ~configuration menu~@Config@.


